   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "In the following example, I would like to choose the colors for the paths myself.\r<br>How can I do this?\r<br>\r<br>\r<br>\r<br>\r<br>library(ggplot2)\r<br>mydata&lt;-data.frame(x=1:10,y=c(1:5,5:1),g=rep(c(&quot;a&quot;,&quot;b&quot;),each=5))\r<br>qplot(x,y,color=g,data=mydata,geom=&quot;path&quot;)\r<br>\r<br>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "enugbxxRs20J",
   "from": "David Kahle",
   "author": "e4aec126ff1dca22",
   "date": "2012-07-11T16:01:07Z",
   "subject": "Re: Choosing colors",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\">See ?scale_colour_manual.<div><br></div><div>HTH,</div><div>david.</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\"><div><div><br><div><div>On Jul 11, 2012, at 10:57 AM, Neuwirth Erich wrote:</div><br><blockquote type=\"cite\"><span style=\"border-collapse:separate;font-family:Helvetica;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:normal;text-align:-webkit-auto;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;font-size:medium\">library(ggplot2)<br>mydata&lt;-data.frame(x=1:10,y=c(1:5,5:1),g=rep(c(&quot;a&quot;,&quot;b&quot;),each=5))<br>qplot(x,y,color=g,data=mydata,geom=&quot;path&quot;)</span></blockquote></div><br></div></div></div>"
    ]
